al ........ Blacus (Leioblacus) longipetiolatus sp. nov. - Length of first metasomal tergite 2.30 X its apical width; hind tibia length 11.60 X its maximum width hind basitar- sus length 7.50 X its width. Taiwan ........................................................... Blacus (Leioblacus) whartoni Achterberg Blacus longipetiolatus is similar to B. macrocephalus Achterberg, but differs in that the notauli are absent in B. longipetiolatus; the head is also smaller with respect to the height of mesosoma and the first tergite is 3.75 – 5.0 X longer than its apical width in B. longipetiolatus whereas in B. macrocephalus it is 2.7 X longer than apical width.","","text","",""]]},"MLT4":{"d":[["Somalia","","text","",""]]},"MM34":{"d":[["","QLD","tdwg","",""]]},"N6N78":{"d":[["ZA, KwaZulu-Natal","","text","native",""]]},"NGF42":{"d":[["Waigeo (Raja Ampat Islands, off western New Guinea)","","text","",""]]},"NMNX":{"d":[["Angola","","text","",""]]},"NQV57":{"d":[["Denmark","DK","iso","","not evaluated"]]},"NXXC":{"d":[["Micronesia","8595","mrgid","",""],["Saipan","32817","mrgid","",""]]},"P8SF":{"d":[["European waters (ERMS scope)","7130","mrgid","",""],["Madeiran Exclusive Economic Zone","8363","mrgid","",""],["Spain - Demarcación Marina Canaria","62661","mrgid","",""]]},"PKHZD":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"PKLRH":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"PKM9":{"d":[["USA","","text","",""]]},"PLY5W":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"Q43GB":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"QB83C":{"d":[["Indian part of the Bay of Bengal","25430","mrgid","native",""]]},"QSYD":{"d":[["MDG","MDG","tdwg","",""]]},"R2YD":{"d":[["Brazil","","text","",""]]},"R38D":{"d":[["Port Phillip Bay","14934","mrgid","",""]]},"R3YXK":{"d":[["Distribution. This is the rarest Micandra species in Colombia, known from a specimen recently collected in Nariño at 1500 m.","","text","",""],["Distribution. This species is known from the three Andean cordilleras in the 